title: UGC video editing workflow defined as Phase 2 north star
summary: 'Team session defining Atelier''s UGC video workflow scope. User will shoot daily talking-head footage and needs an agent-assisted system to remove editing tedium: multi-take ingestion, silence removal, auto-captions, graphic overlay generation, and a basic timeline for ordering and trimming clips. Atelier is not trying to replace CapCut — it handles the grunt work and produces a clean draft MP4; external tools handle effects, body tracking, color grading if needed. Phase 2 scope updated to include VideoProject folder structure, timeline UI, Whisper transcription, and silence removal. Whisper pulled forward from Phase 3.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#video-renderer'
  - '#cli-lint'
  - '#frame-resolver'
  - '#layer-types'
symbols_created:
  - '#video-project'
  - '#timeline-ui'
  - '#caption-pipeline'
  - '#silence-removal'
  - '#atelier-edit-cli'
decisions:
  - id: ugc-scope-boundary
    decision: Atelier handles ingest, silence removal, captions, basic timeline, graphics, export. External tools (CapCut etc.) handle effects, body tracking, color grading.
    rationale: User explicitly does not want to rebuild CapCut — wants tedium removed, creative control retained, higher-level effects handled by specialized tools
  - id: whisper-phase2
    decision: Pull Whisper auto-caption integration from Phase 3 into Phase 2
    rationale: Captions are core to the UGC daily workflow, not a nice-to-have. Phase 2 without captions would be incomplete for the stated use case
  - id: timeline-basic-only
    decision: Timeline UI covers clip ordering, trim in/out, drag to reorder only. No keyframe curves, effects rack, or multi-track audio.
    rationale: Data model already supports this via startFrame + sourceOffset + sourceEnd. Studio just needs a visual representation. Scope stays tight.
